# AGENTS.md

A murmur app: pieces under `pieces/` talk only through contracts in `contracts/`. Run commands from this folder.
`capabilities/web/capability.ts` is the http token edges bind routes to (`@Serve(web.get('/x/:id'))`), the one place
that lists the default guards (in the order they run) and the input failure map (`errors.input`). Shared pure code lives
in `lib/` and is imported as `#lib/<module>`.

- `pnpm exec murmur ctx pieces/<id>` — the whole brief for one piece; read it instead of the repo.
  `--withhold-code` leaves `piece.ts` out (regenerate it from the brief). `pnpm exec murmur ctx lib/<module>` — one lib
  module.
- `pnpm exec murmur new piece <path>` / `pnpm exec murmur new contract <ClassName> --domain <file> --kind query` /
  `pnpm exec murmur new lib <name>` — scaffolds (`--kind guard` + `new piece <path> --handles <Guard>` for a guard).
- `pnpm exec murmur check pieces/<id>` — structure, boundaries, sizing; `pnpm exec murmur test pieces/<id>` — tests.
- `pnpm exec murmur catalog` — who emits and handles what.
- `pnpm exec murmur dev` runs the app; `pnpm exec murmur tail`, `trace <id>` and `emit <Contract>` talk to it.
- `pnpm exec murmur migrate` applies the `schema.sql` files; `pnpm exec murmur start [process]` runs it in production.
